<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="light">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="description" content="Meet the Prompt Engineers Who Can't Center a Div: five computer science students thinking carefully about AI and software engineering.">
  <title>Team The Prompt Engineers Who Can't Center a Div | Agentic SE Lab</title>
  <script>
    (() => {
      let theme;
      try {
        theme = localStorage.getItem("upb-theme");
      } catch (_) {}
      if (theme !== "light" && theme !== "dark") {
        theme = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light";
      }
      document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
    })();
  </script>
  <style>
    :root {
      --accent: #E4007C;
    }

    [data-theme="light"] {
      color-scheme: light;
      --bg: #FFF8E7;
      --text: #1D1D1F;
      --secondary: #5A5A5F;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      --border: #E8E1D3;
      --shadow: 0 0.5rem 1.5rem rgba(29, 29, 31, 0.08);
    }

    [data-theme="dark"] {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #14142B;
      --text: #F4F1DE;
      --secondary: #B8B5A7;
      --card: #1F1F3D;
      --border: #383858;
      --shadow: 0 0.5rem 1.5rem rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    html {
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      background: var(--bg);
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--bg);
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      transition: background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    a {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
    }

    a:focus-visible,
    button:focus-visible {
      outline: 0.2rem solid var(--accent);
      outline-offset: 0.2rem;
    }

    .site-header {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }

    .header-inner {
      position: relative;
      max-width: 70rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 2rem;
    }

    .header-copy {
      max-width: 49rem;
      padding-right: 5rem;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      line-height: 1.12;
      letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    }

    .tagline {
      margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .site-nav {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin-top: 1.1rem;
    }

    #theme-toggle {
      position: absolute;
      top: 2.5rem;
      right: 1.5rem;
      display: inline-flex;
      min-width: 2.75rem;
      min-height: 2.75rem;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      border: 2px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--accent);
      font: inherit;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      cursor: pointer;
      transition: background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
    }

    #theme-toggle:hover {
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #FFFFFF;
    }

    main {
      max-width: 70rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 2.5rem 1.5rem 3rem;
    }

    section + section {
      margin-top: 4rem;
    }

    h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      line-height: 1.25;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    }

    .section-intro {
      max-width: 48rem;
      margin: 0.65rem 0 1.75rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .member-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .member-card {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      transition: background-color 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease;
    }

    .member-card img {
      display: block;
      width: 8rem;
      height: 8rem;
      margin: 0 auto 1rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 50%;
      object-fit: cover;
    }

    h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }

    .study {
      margin: 0.35rem 0 0.8rem;
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .bio,
    .fun-fact,
    .future-view {
      margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    }

    .future-view {
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .future-view strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .fun-fact {
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    .hot-take {
      margin: auto 0 0;
      padding: 0.7rem 0.8rem;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #FFFFFF;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      font-weight: 650;
      line-height: 1.45;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .future-panel {
      max-width: 58rem;
      padding: 1.75rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 1rem;
      background: var(--card);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .future-panel p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    .future-panel p + p {
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .future-note {
      color: var(--secondary);
    }

    footer {
      padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--secondary);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .header-inner {
        padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
      }

      .header-copy {
        padding-right: 3.5rem;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      #theme-toggle {
        top: 1.25rem;
        right: 1rem;
      }

      .site-nav {
        margin-top: 1rem;
      }

      main {
        padding: 2rem 1rem 2.5rem;
      }

      .member-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      section + section {
        margin-top: 3rem;
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      *,
      *::before,
      *::after {
        scroll-behavior: auto !important;
        transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="header-inner">
      <div class="header-copy">
        <h1>The Prompt Engineers Who Can't Center a Div</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Five computer scientists, many agents, and a healthy respect for the review button.</p>
        <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="#team">Meet the team</a>
          <a href="#future-of-se">Our view on the future</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <button id="theme-toggle" type="button" aria-label="Switch to night mode">☾</button>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section id="team" aria-labelledby="team-heading">
      <h2 id="team-heading">The humans behind the prompts</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">All five of us are pursuing an M.Sc. in Computer Science at Paderborn University. We like building things, asking what could go wrong, and occasionally asking an agent to explain its own code.</p>

      <div class="member-grid">
        <article class="member-card">
          <img src="{{image:Harsh.png}}" alt="Photo of Harsh">
          <h3>Harsh</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, Paderborn University; B.E. Computer Engineering</p>
          <p class="bio">Harsh is pursuing his master's after a B.E. in Computer Engineering. Machine learning, football and ambitious cooking experiments keep him busy. He finds AI surprisingly good at explaining code and writing tests, but it often misses why a system was built a certain way. His approach: bring the human context. Looking ahead, he expects developers to manage small teams of agents, breaking work into clear tasks and checking the results quickly.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: He has more half-finished ML side projects than finished meals this semester.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Most “AI bugs” are just human requirements that were never written down.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img src="{{image:Keval.png}}" alt="Photo of Keval">
          <h3>Keval</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, Paderborn University; B.E. Computer Engineering</p>
          <p class="bio">Keval is studying for an M.Sc. after earning a B.E. in Computer Engineering. Cloud and DevOps, cricket, and long rides along the Lippe are his kind of downtime. He likes AI for scripts, configs and decoding error messages, but knows it can suggest insecure shortcuts; security and operations still need human judgment. In five to ten years, he expects agents to deploy and fix systems, while engineers set the permissions, tests and rollback plans that keep them safe.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: His CI pipeline has a better success rate than his alarm clock.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 Giving an AI agent production access without a sandbox is just chaos engineering with extra steps.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img src="{{image:Krish.png}}" alt="Photo of Krish">
          <h3>Krish</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, Paderborn University; B.E. Computer Engineering</p>
          <p class="bio">Krish is pursuing an M.Sc. in Computer Science after a B.E. in Computer Engineering. He builds side projects and follows cricket, sometimes debugging late with a little too much chai. AI assistants save him time on boilerplate and first drafts, especially when he already knows what he wants, but a person who understands the system still has to check the work. He expects engineers to spend less time typing and more time specifying, reviewing and testing what agents produce.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: He once fixed a production bug from his phone while waiting in a supermarket queue.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 The best prompt engineer on your team is just the person who writes the clearest tickets.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img src="{{image:Nevil.png}}" alt="Photo of Nevil">
          <h3>Nevil</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, Paderborn University; B.E. Computer Engineering</p>
          <p class="bio">Nevil is pursuing his M.Sc. after studying Computer Engineering for his B.E. He enjoys frontend and UI design, photography and badminton—and might spend a while choosing a palette. AI can make a working interface quickly, but working is not the same as pleasant: accessibility, design and the details users notice still need a human eye. In five to ten years, he thinks building will feel more like directing, with taste, empathy and clear communication doing more work than framework trivia.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: He spends more time picking a colour palette than writing the actual code.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 AI can center a div on the first try, which already makes it better than half of us.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="member-card">
          <img src="{{image:Nirav.png}}" alt="Photo of Nirav">
          <h3>Nirav</h3>
          <p class="study">M.Sc. Computer Science, Paderborn University; B.E. Computer Engineering</p>
          <p class="bio">Nirav is studying for an M.Sc. after completing a B.E. in Computer Engineering. He likes backend systems, table tennis and exploring street-food stalls in new places. AI feels like a tireless junior developer: useful for boilerplate, but not always inclined to say “I’m not sure.” Nirav reads every line before it reaches main. He expects code-writing to become the easy part; designing systems, defining correctness and preventing agents from tripping over one another will take the real engineering.</p>
          <p class="fun-fact"><em>Fun fact: He has named every one of his laptops after a Bollywood villain.</em></p>
          <p class="hot-take">🔥 An AI that writes 1,000 lines a minute just means 1,000 lines a minute someone has to review.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="future-of-se" aria-labelledby="future-heading">
      <h2 id="future-heading">The Future of Software Engineering</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Our shared forecast: less typing from scratch, more deciding what “right” means.</p>
      <div class="future-panel">
        <p>AI agents are already useful teammates for boilerplate, tests and first drafts. They still need humans who understand the system, set the direction and check the result. A confident answer is not the same as a correct one—and “it passed once” is not quite a test strategy.</p>
        <p class="future-note">We expect the job to shift from writing code to specifying, reviewing and verifying it. The engineers who thrive will explain clearly what they want, break a problem into sensible pieces and spot quickly when an answer is wrong. Agents may do more of the implementation; people will still own the context, the trade-offs and the consequences. In short: delegate the typing, not the thinking.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    Built by an agent, supervised by humans. <span id="current-year"></span> · The Prompt Engineers Who Can't Center a Div
  </footer>

  <script>
    (() => {
      const root = document.documentElement;
      const toggle = document.getElementById("theme-toggle");

      function updateButton() {
        const isDark = root.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark";
        toggle.textContent = isDark ? "☀" : "☾";
        toggle.setAttribute("aria-label", isDark ? "Switch to day mode" : "Switch to night mode");
      }

      updateButton();
      toggle.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const nextTheme = root.getAttribute("data-theme") === "dark" ? "light" : "dark";
        root.setAttribute("data-theme", nextTheme);
        try {
          localStorage.setItem("upb-theme", nextTheme);
        } catch (_) {}
        updateButton();
      });

      document.getElementById("current-year").textContent = new Date().getFullYear();
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

